  "agent_summary": "2 nutrients are above the upper limit (UL) for a 34-year-old female from these supplements alone. Magnesium: 575 mg a day vs a UL of 350 mg (164%), mostly from Natrol Magnesium Night High Absorption 325 mg Naturally Flavored. The UL guards against diarrhea and other gastrointestinal upset from supplemental magnesium. Vitamin D: 150 mcg a day vs a UL of 100 mcg (150%), mostly from Natural Healthy Concepts Vitamin D3 Concepts 5000. The UL guards against high blood calcium (hypercalcemia), which can lead to kidney stones and calcification of soft tissues. Leaving out Custom magnesium would bring magnesium to 325 mg (92.9% of the UL), still near it. Totals exclude food, drinks and medications. Label data, not medical advice.",
  "assumptions": [
    "dsld:230932: servings_per_day not given; used label maximum of 1 (label: 1 Softgel(s), 1 time(s) daily)",
    "dsld:338022: servings_per_day not given; used label maximum of 1 (label: 1 Tablet(s), 1 time(s) daily)",
    "dsld:332278: servings_per_day not given; used label maximum of 1 (label: 7.7 Gram(s), 1 time(s) daily)",
    "custom:1: servings_per_day not given; amounts treated as one serving per day",
    "Totals cover the listed supplements only; food, beverages and medications are not included.",
    "The UL for Calcium, Copper, Iodine, Iron, Phosphorus, Selenium, Vitamin B6, Vitamin C, Vitamin D and Zinc applies to total intake from food and supplements; a supplement total under the UL does not show that total intake is under it.",
    "coverage compares supplement totals alone with the RDA (or AI); diet normally supplies much of the reference amount, so low coverage does not indicate a shortfall."
  ],
